Package distributions retain their own notices and license files.

LLMs allowed by the case, accessed only through the organizer's external API:
Gemma 4 26B A4B; GLM-5.3-Flash; Qwen3.6 35B A3B;
DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash; Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct; Kimi-K2.6.
No model weights are redistributed. Provider terms, model licenses, API IDs
and tariffs must be verified against organizer-supplied documentation.
Default live configuration selects Qwen3.6 35B A3B and Gemma 4 26B A4B.
Demo mode does not call a model.

External sources configured: Bank of Russia public RSS and Vedomosti public
RSS/open pages. Publisher rights remain with their owners. Access does not
grant republication rights; retain attribution and follow publisher terms.
Restricted/paywalled articles are not bypassed.

Synthetic datasets and simulated integrations:
- Three fictional companies, fabricated payment links, events and analytical
  examples in app/seed.py and data/demo/. None identify real clients.
- data/evaluation/events.json: synthetic evaluation scaffold, unreviewed labels.
- Internet banking UI and logins simulate a corporate bank cabinet.
- CSVs from the organizer, actual Alfa-Bank research, bank SSO, payment systems,
  actual model API and an external deployment are not bundled.
- Lexical retrieval, scoring and demo interpretations are project-owned rules.
